# KopiTehnik Print Free-Use License, version 0.1 (DRAFT)

Copyright (c) 2026 ildargiv. All rights reserved except as granted below.

NOTE: this is a plain-language draft and has not been reviewed by a lawyer.

## 1. Free use

You may use, copy and run KopiTehnik Print ("the Software") **free of charge, including commercially**, as long as the Software is used on **one workstation (one computer) at one business location**. Personal and non-commercial use, on any number of your own computers, is always free.

## 2. When you need a commercial licence

You need a paid commercial licence from the author if you:
- use the Software on **more than one workstation** in a business, or at **more than one location**;
- are a chain, franchise or other multi-site operator;
- provide the Software to your customers or other businesses as part of a product or service, or sell, rent or bundle it.

Contact the author through the project page on GitHub to obtain a commercial licence.

## 3. Daily volume

Heavy-use businesses are expected to hold a commercial licence. Future versions of the Software may show a notice when the number of sheets printed in a day exceeds a stated threshold, and may stop printing above a higher threshold. Printing is not blocked below that higher threshold.

## 4. Source and changes

The source code is published for transparency and for you to inspect and build the Software for your own permitted use. You may make changes for your own permitted use. You may not distribute modified or unmodified copies, or builds, except the official releases unchanged, and you may not use the name "KopiTehnik Print" or its logo for a modified version.

## 5. No cracking

You may not remove, disable or bypass any licence notice, counter or limit in the Software.

## 6. Notices

Anyone who gets a copy of the Software from you must also get a copy of this licence.

## 7. Third-party components

The Software uses third-party libraries and models that stay under their own licences.

## 8. No warranty

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND. THE AUTHOR IS NOT LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY ARISING FROM THE USE OF THE SOFTWARE.

## 9. Earlier versions

Versions released before this licence took effect remain available under the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 (https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0). You may choose either licence for those versions.

## 10. Termination

If you breach this licence, your rights under it end until you stop the breach.
